    },
    {
      "id": "1b141d7e-ef55-45df-b78b-bc1b928828c8",
      "noteId": "e90d4692-4430-44b0-8497-d0668d30acec",
      "position": 16,
      "type": "QUOTE",
      "text": "HALO-QA-20261029 EVAPORATION. Evaporation changes liquid water into water vapour. It can occur below the boiling point because some surface molecules have enough energy to escape. Adding heat supplies energy to the molecules and usually makes evaporation faster. Boiling forms bubbles throughout a liquid at its boiling point, while evaporation happens at the surface. Moving air removes water vapour",
      "checked": 0,
      "indent": 0,
      "refObjectId": null,
      "language": null,
