    {
      "id": "a6b1ff8b-81de-482a-9d6d-84b08d770d6d",
      "noteId": "e90d4692-4430-44b0-8497-d0668d30acec",
      "position": 19,
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "text": "**Hint**\nBoth processes turn liquid into vapour, but they differ in location. Evaporation only involves surface molecules, while boiling creates bubbles from the bulk liquid.",
      "checked": 0,
      "indent": 0,
      "refObjectId": null,
      "language": null,
      "createdAtEpochMs": 1793358889628,
      "updatedAtEpochMs": 1793358889628
    },
    {
      "id": "7f541f28-da17-4328-a824-04542dd3c807",
      "noteId": "e90d4692-4430-44b0-8497-d0668d30acec",
      "position": 20,
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "text": "**Why**\nThe source states evaporation “can occur below the boiling point because some surface molecules have enough energy to escape.” Boiling “forms bubbles throughout a liquid at its boiling point.” Thus, evaporation happens at the surface, boiling occurs throughout.",
      "checked": 0,
      "indent": 0,
      "refObjectId": null,
      "language": null,
      "createdAtEpochMs": 1793358889628,
      "updatedAtEpochMs": 1793358889628
    },
    {
      "id": "41da1d16-368d-4393-9f4c-c390fdeb0d98",
      "noteId": "e90d4692-4430-44b0-8497-d0668d30acec",
      "position": 21,
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "text": "**Next step**\nImagine a pot on a stove. At what temperature do bubbles first appear throughout the water? Your answer may cite [source].\nИсточник: HALO-QA-20261029 EVAPORATION. Evaporation changes liquid water into water vapour · Версия 12 · Выбранный отрывок · символы 0–444",
      "checked": 0,
      "indent": 0,
