    {
      "id": "aa4765ea-7157-418f-b7e0-8355e5adc29d",
      "noteId": "e90d4692-4430-44b0-8497-d0668d30acec",
      "position": 24,
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "text": "**Hint**\nThe source links heat to energy for escaping molecules, and moving air to removing vapour near the surface.",
      "checked": 0,
      "indent": 0,
      "refObjectId": null,
      "language": null,
      "createdAtEpochMs": 1793358889628,
      "updatedAtEpochMs": 1793358889628
    },
    {
      "id": "f3f9c161-b9fb-4767-8318-51a86e1e3ce2",
      "noteId": "e90d4692-4430-44b0-8497-d0668d30acec",
      "position": 25,
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "text": "**Why**\n[source] states: “Adding heat supplies energy to the molecules and usually makes evaporation faster.” It also notes that “Moving air removes water vapour near the surface and can speed evaporation.” Heat raises molecule kinetic energy; airflow strips away vapour so more molecules can leave.",
      "checked": 0,
      "indent": 0,
      "refObjectId": null,
      "language": null,
      "createdAtEpochMs": 1793358889628,
      "updatedAtEpochMs": 1793358889628
    },
    {
      "id": "e3205aef-667c-4610-b14c-42746309c9ee",
      "noteId": "e90d4692-4430-44b0-8497-d0668d30acec",
      "position": 26,
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "text": "**Next step**\nExplain, in one sentence each, how heat and moving air speed evaporation, then contrast their roles. Use only the paragraph and cite [source].\nИсточник: HALO-QA-20261029 EVAPORATION. Evaporation changes liquid water into water vapour · Версия 12 · Выбранный отрывок · символы 0–444",
