    {
      "id": "547a3577-7fd2-471a-ad16-7d07593deeaf",
      "noteId": "e90d4692-4430-44b0-8497-d0668d30acec",
      "position": 31,
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "text": "What happens to some surface water molecules during evaporation below the boiling point?\nSome surface molecules have enough energy to escape.",
      "checked": 0,
      "indent": 0,
      "refObjectId": null,
      "language": null,
      "createdAtEpochMs": 1793358889628,
      "updatedAtEpochMs": 1793358889628
    },
    {
      "id": "72309dec-b0a2-4f15-a311-5246ca372dd7",
      "noteId": "e90d4692-4430-44b0-8497-d0668d30acec",
      "position": 32,
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "text": "How does moving air affect the rate of evaporation?\nMoving air removes water vapour near the surface and can speed evaporation.",
      "checked": 0,
      "indent": 0,
      "refObjectId": null,
      "language": null,
      "createdAtEpochMs": 1793358889628,
      "updatedAtEpochMs": 1793358889628
    },
    {
      "id": "41293f48-b3b5-49a7-b1d6-42ef15dfefe7",
      "noteId": "e90d4692-4430-44b0-8497-d0668d30acec",
      "position": 33,
      "type": "PARAGRAPH",
      "text": "What is the difference between evaporation and boiling in terms of where the process occurs?\nEvaporation happens at the surface, while boiling forms bubbles throughout a liquid at its boiling point.",
      "checked": 0,
      "indent": 0,
      "refObjectId": null,
      "language": null,
      "createdAtEpochMs": 1793358889628,
